# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe BricsCAD batch ignores the --dwg drawing option
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-21

* Observed

Windows, BricsCAD V25 fr_FR, alfe 2.3.15 (SBCL executable). Discovered while
automating SCHMS+ export from =export/test/Exemple Export.dwg= in the sibling
SCHMS checkout.

=--dwg= was supplied with an existing private copy of the fixture, but the
session ran on =Dessin1=. The requested drawing was absent from the launch
arguments. Adding =--epure= does not make the requested drawing take effect.

This is consequential for CAD tests: the transport can report success while
the test operates on a blank drawing instead of the requested fixture.

* Reproduction

Use an existing nonempty =fixture.dwg= and clear drawing/template environment
overrides before running (example for Git Bash on Windows):

#+begin_src sh
env -u AUTOLISP_DWG -u AUTOLISP_BRICSCAD_TEMPLATE \
  alfe -norc --bricscad --mode batch --dwg fixture.dwg \
  -x '(print (getvar "DWGNAME"))' \
  -x '(print (getvar "DWGPREFIX"))' --quit
#+end_src

Expected: =fixture.dwg= and the directory of the supplied file. Observed in
the SCHMS run: =Dessin1=, with no requested fixture in the process command
line. Repeat with =--epure= on a configured workstation; EPURE can add its
own startup effects, so isolate the basic backend test first.

The SCHMS diagnostic run passed these relevant options:

#+begin_example
alfe -norc --bricscad --epure --mode batch --timeout 600
     --workdir <private-run>/alfe --keep-workdir
     --dwg <private-run>/Exemple Export.dwg
     -Esource WINDOWS-1252 -l <private-run>/run.lsp --quit -q
#+end_example

* Source evidence

- =autolisp-front-end/source/cli.lisp= forwards =cli-options-dwg= to
  =start-engine= as =:dwg=.
- =autolisp-front-end/source/backend-bricscad.lisp= accepts =dwg= in
  =start-engine= but declares it ignored. Its template discovery path does
  not forward it as the =requested= argument.
- =discover-bricscad-template= documents an explicit requested drawing as
  the highest-precedence input, but the CLI value never reaches that path.

* Workaround verified

Setting =AUTOLISP_BRICSCAD_TEMPLATE= to the private fixture made the file
appear in the BricsCAD process command line and opened the actual drawing.
The SCHMS launcher also set =AUTOLISP_DWG=; this is a workaround, not a fix
for the CLI option. EPURE's separate interactive migration on opening an old
fixture then became visible; that is a different bootstrap issue.

* Acceptance

- Forward the requested drawing through BricsCAD template resolution before
  considering a cached/default/vendor template.
- An explicit =--dwg= must win over environment template/drawing defaults.
- Add a backend regression checking the actual launch arguments, including
  a pathname containing spaces and a pre-populated backend template cache.
- An explicitly missing drawing must fail rather than silently fall back
  to a blank/vendor drawing.
- Verify on BricsCAD that =DWGNAME= and =DWGPREFIX= identify the requested
  file, both with and without the EPURE plugin where available.
- Do not change AutoCAD or clautolisp drawing selection incidentally.
